---
import { cta } from '../../lib/site';
---

<section class="container-page pt-14 pb-section-tight lg:pt-24">
	<p class="anim-enter eyebrow">For independent caterers and small kitchen teams</p>
	<div class="mt-5 grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[7fr_5fr] lg:gap-16">
		<div>
			<h1 class="anim-enter max-w-[19ch] text-[clamp(2.375rem,1.5rem+3vw,4rem)] leading-[1.04] font-semibold" style="--enter-delay: 70ms">
				Know what every event should cost before you quote it.
			</h1>
			<p class="anim-enter mt-6 max-w-[62ch] text-lede text-ink-soft" style="--enter-delay: 150ms">
				CostCook connects the prices you pay to ingredients, recipes, menus, and orders.
				Choose a costed menu, enter the guest count and selling price, and see the event&rsquo;s
				theoretical food cost, what still needs to be bought, and what Shop, Prep, and Pack
				need next.
			</p>
			<div class="anim-enter mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-3" style="--enter-delay: 230ms">
				<a
					href={cta.href}
					target={cta.target}
					rel={cta.rel}
					aria-label={cta.ariaLabel}
					class="btn-primary"
				>
					{cta.label}
				</a>
				<a href="#chain" class="btn-quiet">See the costing chain <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
			</div>
			<p class="anim-enter mt-5 text-sm text-ink-soft" style="--enter-delay: 290ms">
				Bring one real menu or order. Nothing to install.
			</p>
		</div>

		<figure class="anim-enter-settle" style="--enter-delay: 260ms">
			<picture>
				<source media="(max-width: 639px)" srcset="/proof/money-mobile.png" />
				<img
					src="/proof/money.png"
					alt="A CostCook order comparison showing the frozen quoted food cost beside the same order at current ingredient prices."
					width="2528"
					height="430"
					fetchpriority="high"
					decoding="async"
					class="h-auto w-full bg-paper shadow-ticket"
				/>
			</picture>
			<figcaption class="mt-4 max-w-md text-sm text-ink-soft">
				A confirmed order keeps the numbers that were quoted while current prices continue
				moving future work.
			</figcaption>
		</figure>
	</div>
</section>
